          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came in with palpitations and breathlessness.\n\nThe team found:\n- New atrial fibrillation (AF) with a fast heart rate\n- Mild decompensated heart failure"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "On Day 1, the team checked your heart rate and blood pressure and examined you.\n\nThe team:\n- Gave treatment to slow your heart rate\n- Continued your anticoagulation (blood-thinning treatment)\n- Started treatment to remove excess fluid\n\nOn Day 2, the team loaded a medicine to control your heart rate (digoxin). Your heart rate improved.\n\nOn Day 2, a beta-blocker (bisoprolol) was increased to 5mg once a day."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.8",
            "sections.9"
          ],
          "text": "You have a cardiology follow-up appointment at 6 weeks.\n\nYour GP will:\n- Monitor your INR\n- Monitor your digoxin level"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
